-- search.talk: the lazily-stays-on-its-element case (spec chapter 8,
-- Compiling). `lazily` swaps only the splits of its element's own
-- repetition, never those inside a nested `<…>`.

script variable outer = nothing
script variable plain = nothing

on go
  put every match of <"#", one or more of <digits> lazily> in "#123" into outer
  put every match of <"#", digits lazily> in "#123" into plain
end go
